meta {
  name: 00 READ ME first
  type: http
  seq: 0
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  B2 as a second CEFR level — phase 26.

  WHAT THIS CHECKS
  A B2 seat gets the whole Start experience on Modelltest 7, and a centre
  can run a B2 Exam Day sitting that is timed and marked as B2 rather than
  as B1.

  BEFORE YOU START
  1. Run the API against the disposable database, not production:
         .\scripts\start-dev-testdb.ps1
     It prints the database host. It must NOT be ep-wandering-hall.
  2. Modelltest 7 must be imported on that database:
         npm run modelltest:verify -- --level B2 --number 7
     Expect "Modelltest 7 (B2) verified."
  3. A centre signed in (Center Auth / 03 Login) so {{accessToken}} is set,
     and an activation code minted so {{codeId}} is set.
  4. TWO students, not one:
       {{studentAccessToken}}    on a seat set to B2  (requests 01-02)
       {{b1StudentAccessToken}}  on a seat left at B1
     The B1 student is what requests 05 and 07b need, and they are the only
     two that prove a level gate exists rather than that B2 content exists.

  ORDER
  Requests run in seq order, which is now strictly increasing with no
  duplicates. It did not used to be: six pairs shared a seq, and two of them
  — the sitting edit and the Hoeren timing check — acted on the same sitting
  and asserted opposite levels, so one of the two failed depending on which
  the runner happened to pick first.

  01 and 02 put a B2 student on a seat. Everything after depends on
  {{studentAccessToken}} belonging to that student.

  RE-RUNNING
  Not idempotent. 01 needs a code still in `activated`; a second run is 409
  INVALID_CODE_TRANSITION. Mint a fresh code and reset {{codeId}} before
  running the collection again.

  THE EXAM CHAIN (14a-14h)
  Blocks open in telc order and each must be started AND submitted before
  the next: LESEN_SPRACHBAUSTEINE, then HOEREN, then SCHREIBEN. 14d1-14d4
  do the first two. They are not optional scaffolding — 14d3 is where the
  20-minute Hoeren deadline is asserted, which is the one value that
  separates B2 from B1.

  WHAT WOULD HAVE FAILED BEFORE THIS PHASE
  - 10 Live Room: 400, because the level validator accepted only B1
  - 12 Create B2 sitting: level stamped B1 whatever paper was chosen
  - 14d3 Hoeren 20 minutes: timed with B1's 30
  - 07 Schreiben both tasks: only one of the two offered
  - 09 Vocab pack: empty
}
